<title>USA: Environmental Technologies CEO resigns.</title>
<headline>Environmental Technologies CEO resigns.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Environmental Technologies USA Inc said Monday Jeffrey Lee has resigned as chief executive officer of the company.</p>
<p>Lee assumed the post of chief executive after the resignation of Robin Young in August. A spokesman for Environmental Technologies said the board has not taken any action yet to fill the vacancy.</p>
<p>Lee will remain president and CEO of the company's carpet recycling unit, United Recycling.</p>
<p>Environmental Technologies converts used consumer and commercial carpeting into fibers for use in thermoplastic and non-woven textile applications.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
